From 7bde8081cc61844b7f62d61dc3350e27d0ee8461 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:44:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): scale three-finger swipe travel per axis via
 [input.gesture] travel_scale_*
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three-finger travel arrives pointer-accelerated, so the same physical swipe
covers more distance when the fingers move fast. travel_scale_horizontal and
travel_scale_vertical scale how far swipes along each axis move content —
strip pans and workspace switching, on the desktop and in the overview alike
(1.0 keeps the upstream distances) — without touching pointer speed, window
drag, or window resize. The per-axis split lets each axis be tuned for its
role: where swiping one way pans the strip and the other switches workspaces,
the two distances scale independently.

The same axis value governs the desktop and the overview (the workspace step
and the viewport pan divide by the same scaled travel, latched per gesture),
so one swipe step reads the same distance on either side. Two-finger scroll
arrives unaccelerated and is untouched, as are the four-finger overview
gesture and gestures forwarded to applications. The headless backend cannot
inject three-finger swipes, so the scales are pinned by config_load and
gesture-physics unit tests instead of a harness check.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
